NAME
       stat - display file status

SYNOPSIS
       stat [-t] [-c FORMAT] FILE...

DESCRIPTION
       Display size, type, inode, permissions, owner and timestamps of each
       FILE.

OPTIONS
       -c, --format=FORMAT
           use FORMAT: %n name, %s size, %a octal mode, %A mode string, %F
           type, %u/%U uid/user, %g/%G gid/group, %i inode, %h links, %X/%Y/%Z
           access/modify/change time in seconds

       -t
           print the information in terse form

EXAMPLES
       stat /bin/ls
       stat -c '%n %s bytes' *.c

SEE ALSO
       ls(1), touch(1)
